WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.567
-Jay Pharoah, welcome back.
It's always great to see you.

00:00:03.567 --> 00:00:05.467
-Yeah, it's great to be here.
-Thank you for coming back.

00:00:05.467 --> 00:00:08.133
-Thank you.
-Last time you were on the show,

00:00:08.133 --> 00:00:10.534
you did a great impression
of Dwayne Johnson.

00:00:10.534 --> 00:00:11.634
-Yeah. Mm-hmm.

00:00:11.634 --> 00:00:13.934
-We had Dwayne on the show...
-Uh-huh.

00:00:13.934 --> 00:00:17.734
-...and played the impression
for Dwayne to see his reaction.

00:00:17.734 --> 00:00:20.734
And he loved it.
-Yeah, he was --

00:00:20.734 --> 00:00:22.133
-He loved it.
-Yeah, he --

00:00:22.133 --> 00:00:24.334
Dwayne has always been --
Y'all got to under--

00:00:24.334 --> 00:00:26.834
When I was a little kid,
I used to want to be The Rock.

00:00:26.834 --> 00:00:29.234
I was -- I told --
-I still want to be The Rock.

00:00:29.234 --> 00:00:30.434
-Yeah, yeah, yeah,
'cause he's --

00:00:30.434 --> 00:00:32.067
[As The Rock] I mean,
yeah, he's just so cool.

00:00:32.067 --> 00:00:33.534
And, yeah, he's that guy

00:00:33.534 --> 00:00:35.534
that just says things,
and he's like --

00:00:35.534 --> 00:00:37.300
Yeah, you know,
he's just a great guy.

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:39.601
And, uh...
Yeah, it's just...

00:00:39.601 --> 00:00:41.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:41.968 --> 00:00:44.200
-[Normal voice] It was
so crazy because I went --

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:46.501
I went to
the "Black Adam" premiere,

00:00:46.501 --> 00:00:48.300
and, you know,
I went there to support him.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:52.701
Also, Aldis Hodge
and also Mo Amer.

00:00:52.701 --> 00:00:54.868
And I saw Dwayne
walking past me,

00:00:54.868 --> 00:00:56.100
and I said,
"Yo, man, what's up?"

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:57.567
-He was like --
[As The Rock] "Hey, come here.

00:00:57.567 --> 00:01:00.367
Me and Jimmy
were just talking about you."

00:01:00.367 --> 00:01:02.000
And he said,
"I'll send you the bill."

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:04.067
[Normal voice] I said,
"What is he talking about?"

00:01:04.067 --> 00:01:06.467
I had one of those, you know --

00:01:06.467 --> 00:01:07.901
You remember
"Diff'rent Strokes"?

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:09.734
Is that what it's called?
"Diff'rent Strokes" with...

00:01:09.734 --> 00:01:11.400
-Arnold.
-Yeah. Yeah, yeah.

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:12.634
And then, you know --
Whatchu talkin' about, Willis?

00:01:12.634 --> 00:01:14.868
I was like, "Whatchu
talkin' about, Dwayne?"

00:01:14.868 --> 00:01:17.367
'Cause I didn't know
what he meant.

00:01:17.367 --> 00:01:19.634
But he --
he was talking about the show.

00:01:19.634 --> 00:01:22.167
He said --
That was so nice of him.

00:01:22.167 --> 00:01:24.300
And I didn't know
until my Twitter blew up,

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:26.267
and people were like,
"Dwayne just said your name!"

00:01:26.267 --> 00:01:29.133
My grandmother was like,
"Dwayne just said your name."

00:01:29.133 --> 00:01:31.234
-Yeah, that's a good thing.

00:01:31.234 --> 00:01:33.167
You know, you do
so many great impressions.

00:01:33.167 --> 00:01:35.634
And you were telling me
backstage that you got cast

00:01:35.634 --> 00:01:37.667
in a Steven Soderbergh movie.
-Absolutely.

00:01:37.667 --> 00:01:40.100
I got cast
in a Steven Soderbergh movie

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:41.434
called "Unsane."

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:42.767
If you haven't seen it,
check it out.

00:01:42.767 --> 00:01:44.334
But I got cast in that movie

00:01:44.334 --> 00:01:46.901
off of my Denzel Washington
impression

00:01:46.901 --> 00:01:48.234
because back --
[ Light applause ]

00:01:48.234 --> 00:01:49.634
Yeah, real talk.
I mean, I heard the clap.

00:01:49.634 --> 00:01:51.367
You can clap. It's fine.
You know?

00:01:51.367 --> 00:01:53.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:53.067 --> 00:01:55.834
A little clap.
There was a little clap.

00:01:55.834 --> 00:01:59.033
So, what happened was,
Matt Damon showed

00:01:59.033 --> 00:02:01.934
Steven Soderbergh
my Denzel Washington impression.

00:02:01.934 --> 00:02:05.067
And, you know, Soderbergh
looked at it, and he said,

00:02:05.067 --> 00:02:07.701
[As Soderbergh] "Well,
that's good. Yeah, I like that."

00:02:07.701 --> 00:02:12.133
So after -- he -- Years later --
It had to be -- It was 2017.

00:02:12.133 --> 00:02:14.634
He hit me up about this movie,
and he said,

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:17.100
"I could tell that
you have dramatic chops

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:19.234
by looking at you doing
that Denzel impression.

00:02:19.234 --> 00:02:21.567
Because to be able to capture
a character like that,

00:02:21.567 --> 00:02:24.267
you have to be able
to act like somebody else."

00:02:24.267 --> 00:02:27.434
And that -- So off of
my Denzel impression --

00:02:27.434 --> 00:02:29.434
Off the Denzel impression,
I booked it.

00:02:29.434 --> 00:02:31.734
[As Denzel] Yeah. I booked it
with Steven Soderbergh.

00:02:31.734 --> 00:02:34.100
That's what I did, huh?
Okay. Alright.

00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:36.834
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.834 --> 00:02:39.234
-That's so wild, bud.
-[Normal voice] Yeah, yeah.

00:02:39.234 --> 00:02:41.968
-You have --
You have over 200 impressions.

00:02:41.968 --> 00:02:44.133
-Absolutely.
-And last time you were

00:02:44.133 --> 00:02:46.634
on the show, I challenged you
to do as many impressions

00:02:46.634 --> 00:02:48.267
as you could in 60 seconds.
-Yeah.

00:02:48.267 --> 00:02:50.100
And I was just wondering
if you'd be up

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:52.100
for doing it again
with different impressions.

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:54.400
-I don't know. This is...
-Come on.

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:56.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:56.434 --> 00:02:59.901
-I'll do it. I'll do it. Yeah.
I can do it.

00:02:59.901 --> 00:03:02.367
-So, what we'll do is...

00:03:02.367 --> 00:03:03.801
we'll put 60 seconds
on the clock,

00:03:03.801 --> 00:03:06.133
and I will prompt you with
different names in no order.

00:03:06.133 --> 00:03:07.300
I'm just gonna go off --

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:08.834
These are names
I got off the website

00:03:08.834 --> 00:03:10.300
that say -- that I heard
that you can do.

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:12.300
-Okay.
-Okay. Are you ready for this?

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:14.667
-Yeah. Yeah.
-60 seconds with Jay Pharoah.

00:03:14.667 --> 00:03:16.667
-Whew!
-Tracy Morgan.

00:03:16.667 --> 00:03:18.234
-[As Morgan]
Hey, that's impossible.

00:03:18.234 --> 00:03:19.868
Why would I do that one?

00:03:19.868 --> 00:03:21.767
Everybody's getting pregnant.

00:03:21.767 --> 00:03:24.133
-Uh, Nicolas Cage.

00:03:24.133 --> 00:03:25.734
-[As Cage]
You know what, Jimmy?

00:03:25.734 --> 00:03:28.234
You're so good
at impersonations.

00:03:28.234 --> 00:03:30.601
And this one is just like that.

00:03:30.601 --> 00:03:32.334
Aha! Alright. Next.

00:03:32.334 --> 00:03:34.334
-Stewie from "Family Guy."
-[As Stewie] Oh, yes.

00:03:34.334 --> 00:03:36.234
Jimmy, we're gonna have
a sexy party,

00:03:36.234 --> 00:03:38.033
and everyone's
going to come here.

00:03:38.033 --> 00:03:39.634
Yakety yak yak yak.
-Chris Tucker.

00:03:39.634 --> 00:03:42.200
-[As Tucker] Hey, man, I don't
even know why you gonna ask me

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:44.767
that, man.
That's crazy, man. Insane, man!

00:03:44.767 --> 00:03:46.868
-President --
President Joe Biden.

00:03:46.868 --> 00:03:48.133
-[As Pres. Biden]
It's just -- Come on, man.

00:03:48.133 --> 00:03:49.400
Just ridiculous, man.

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:51.133
Everybody needs
to get vaccinated.

00:03:51.133 --> 00:03:52.434
Now, if you get vaccinated,

00:03:52.434 --> 00:03:53.934
we'll have something
called herd immunity.

00:03:53.934 --> 00:03:55.801
We'll give you a bag of weed.
Alright.

00:03:55.801 --> 00:03:57.701
-Alright. Jason Statham.

00:03:57.701 --> 00:03:59.200
-[As Statham]
You know, Jason Statham

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:00.734
is that person
that's just like --

00:04:00.734 --> 00:04:03.234
You know, I'm gonna get there,
I'm gonna hit you in the face,

00:04:03.234 --> 00:04:06.367
and I'm gonna tear it off
and I'm gonna eat it. Ergh!

00:04:06.367 --> 00:04:08.033
-John Legend.

00:04:08.033 --> 00:04:10.701
-[As Legend]
♪ We're ordinary people ♪

00:04:10.701 --> 00:04:14.000
♪ We don't know
which way to go... ♪

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:16.901
[ Laughter ]
[Normal voice] Yeah! Yeah!

00:04:16.901 --> 00:04:18.200
[ Bell dinging ]
Come on! Come on! No!

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:20.434
Come on! Come on! Come on!

00:04:20.434 --> 00:04:23.567
You laughed through it!
We had more!

00:04:23.567 --> 00:04:25.033
-I just wanted --
I wanted one more!

00:04:25.033 --> 00:04:26.701
-You have more!

00:04:26.701 --> 00:04:28.267
-There was two more
I wanted to get to. Can I?

00:04:28.267 --> 00:04:29.834
-Come on. Please.
-Do you mind? Bonus?

00:04:29.834 --> 00:04:32.601
-Yeah. No. We have to.
Let's go. Come on.

00:04:32.601 --> 00:04:35.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:35.634 --> 00:04:37.200
Let's do it.
-Chris Rock.

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:38.901
[As Chris Rock]
Oh, come on, man!

00:04:38.901 --> 00:04:40.334
Okay? Okay?

00:04:40.334 --> 00:04:44.367
I got smacked by
the softest person in the world.

00:04:44.367 --> 00:04:45.801
Okay? Okay.

00:04:45.801 --> 00:04:47.267
-Richard Pryor.

00:04:47.267 --> 00:04:50.434
-[As Pryor] Man, that's insane
that you asked me to do Pryor

00:04:50.434 --> 00:04:52.434
'cause I'm on
national television

00:04:52.434 --> 00:04:54.634
and I can't say a damn thing.

00:04:54.634 --> 00:04:56.534
[ Laughter ]

00:04:56.534 --> 00:04:58.434
-John Mulaney.

00:04:58.434 --> 00:05:00.501
-[As Mulaney]
Oh, well, that's crazy, Jimmy.

00:05:00.501 --> 00:05:03.000
You'd ask me
to do John Mulaney.

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:05.133
I'm with Olivia Munn,
and I'm loving it!

00:05:05.133 --> 00:05:06.968
It's amazing.
-Oh, my God.

00:05:06.968 --> 00:05:08.701
-Come on.
That's Jay Pharoah right there.

00:05:08.701 --> 00:05:09.767
Come on, bud.

00:05:09.767 --> 00:05:11.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:11.501 --> 00:05:14.467
♪♪

00:05:14.467 --> 00:05:17.567
-Wow. Wow.

00:05:17.567 --> 00:05:19.934
Thank you for doing that.
-Yeah, man.

00:05:19.934 --> 00:05:21.601
-But is that
what people could see

00:05:21.601 --> 00:05:23.334
when they see you do stand-up?

00:05:23.334 --> 00:05:24.701
-What? What? Just --

00:05:24.701 --> 00:05:26.467
You mean just as far as,
like, impre-- Of course.

00:05:26.467 --> 00:05:29.100
Impressions, yeah,
but now it's like --

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:31.701
It's -- It's morphing, dude.
And it was impression-heavy.

00:05:31.701 --> 00:05:34.100
But I remember
the first time --

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:35.901
I remember killing on stage

00:05:35.901 --> 00:05:37.868
in New York
at Carolines on Broadway.

00:05:37.868 --> 00:05:39.634
And Charlie Murphy
took me there.

00:05:39.634 --> 00:05:40.868
-Carolines is where I --

00:05:40.868 --> 00:05:42.567
It was one of the clubs
I started at, too.

00:05:42.567 --> 00:05:45.167
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
Shout-out to Caroline.

00:05:45.167 --> 00:05:47.000
-Caroline. Caroline Hirsch.
-Yeah. Caroline Hirsch.

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:48.434
And Louis.
-Louis...

00:05:48.434 --> 00:05:50.601
-Louis Faranda.
-Louis Faranda. Yep.

00:05:50.601 --> 00:05:52.167
Caroline Hirsch
and Louis Faranda.

00:05:52.167 --> 00:05:54.400
-They were great.
-Man, I was 19 years old,

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:56.400
and Charlie Murphy took me
on the road with him.

00:05:56.400 --> 00:05:58.400
-Charlie Murphy?
-Yeah. Charlie Murphy.

00:05:58.400 --> 00:05:59.868
[As Murphy]
Y'all know Charlie Murphy, man.

00:05:59.868 --> 00:06:01.267
Talk like this, man.

00:06:01.267 --> 00:06:03.200
[ Laughter ]

00:06:03.200 --> 00:06:04.534
Yeah, he's like, "Yo, son.

00:06:04.534 --> 00:06:06.434
I got to take you
on the road with me, man.

00:06:06.434 --> 00:06:09.367
You hilarious, man. Yeah!"

00:06:09.367 --> 00:06:11.434
[Normal voice] I'm like,
"Is he gonna kill me?

00:06:11.434 --> 00:06:13.767
What is happening?"
-How'd you do?

00:06:13.767 --> 00:06:15.834
-Dude, so,
I got a standing "O"

00:06:15.834 --> 00:06:19.567
the third show Saturday night,
and I didn't expect it.

00:06:19.567 --> 00:06:22.167
I did this Cam'Ron
and Dipset impression,

00:06:22.167 --> 00:06:24.934
which bit -- it killed --
and everybody gets up.

00:06:24.934 --> 00:06:26.467
[ Imitates crowd cheering ]

00:06:26.467 --> 00:06:29.701
And then I trip on stage,
and I was like,

00:06:29.701 --> 00:06:33.667
"No! I don't feel like
it counts anymore!"

00:06:33.667 --> 00:06:35.267
-"I got a standing 'O,'
and then..."

00:06:35.267 --> 00:06:37.634
-I got a standing "O,"
and then -- and then I'm clumsy.

00:06:37.634 --> 00:06:39.000
The clutch just came out.

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:40.868
And I remember
going to the green room.

00:06:40.868 --> 00:06:43.734
And Uncle Ray, Eddie Murphy
and Charlie Murphy's uncle,

00:06:43.734 --> 00:06:45.400
was standing right there,
and he said,

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:48.901
"That was great, but, uh,
we got to work on your balance."

00:06:48.901 --> 00:06:50.801
[ Laughter ]

00:06:50.801 --> 00:06:52.033
Real talk.

00:06:52.033 --> 00:06:53.534
-Just gotta work
on your balance.

00:06:53.534 --> 00:06:55.133
-But it worked out.
-It did work out.

00:06:55.133 --> 00:06:56.701
-It worked out
'cause here you are.

00:06:56.701 --> 00:06:58.634
You're in a big movie.
-Absolutely.

00:06:58.634 --> 00:07:00.434
-Let's talk about
"Spinning Gold."

00:07:00.434 --> 00:07:02.167
-Yeah. "Spinning Gold," man.

00:07:02.167 --> 00:07:04.400
-It's about
the Casablanca Records story?

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:06.000
-It's the story
of Casablanca Records

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:07.634
and Buddah Records.

00:07:07.634 --> 00:07:12.133
And Neil Bogart, who was the
founder of Casablanca Records,

00:07:12.133 --> 00:07:13.534
he, you know -- he came up --

00:07:13.534 --> 00:07:16.067
Donna Summers. KISS.

00:07:16.067 --> 00:07:18.767
Bill Withers.
The Isley Brothers.

00:07:18.767 --> 00:07:21.467
-P-Funk.
-I remember Casablanca Records.

00:07:21.467 --> 00:07:23.534
Donna Summer.
"Bad Girls" record. Yeah.

00:07:23.534 --> 00:07:25.434
-Dude, like, so ma--
I didn't know --

00:07:25.434 --> 00:07:27.033
-Village People.
-Village People.

00:07:27.033 --> 00:07:29.067
Who else is up there?
Kurtis Blow.

00:07:29.067 --> 00:07:30.834
Like, so much history in that.

00:07:30.834 --> 00:07:33.968
And I'm playing Cecil Holmes,
the co-founder --

00:07:33.968 --> 00:07:35.934
the co-founder
of Casablanca Records.

00:07:35.934 --> 00:07:38.834
And he is --
he's the backbone, man.

00:07:38.834 --> 00:07:41.934
Anything Neil Bogart needed,
he was his ride-or-die.

00:07:41.934 --> 00:07:45.734
And I didn't have any footage
or anything to use this time.

00:07:45.734 --> 00:07:49.334
So it was really just me
going off of what Tim Bogart,

00:07:49.334 --> 00:07:51.167
his son,
who directed the film,

00:07:51.167 --> 00:07:55.300
telling me about Cecil
and using personal --

00:07:55.300 --> 00:07:57.601
you know, my personal
relationships to get into it.

00:07:57.601 --> 00:08:00.701
-What years were these set in?
'70s?

00:08:00.701 --> 00:08:04.167
-1970s and top of the '80s.
Yeah, man.

00:08:04.167 --> 00:08:06.968
-Fun time.
-Fun time. Whew!

00:08:06.968 --> 00:08:10.267
-Can't do what you --
Can't do none of that no more.

00:08:10.267 --> 00:08:11.801
-No, no, no, no, no.

00:08:11.801 --> 00:08:13.901
I know there's a --
I want to say there's --

00:08:13.901 --> 00:08:15.934
there's some connection to --
we're gonna show this clip --

00:08:15.934 --> 00:08:18.901
about "The Tonight Show"
and Casablanca Records.

00:08:18.901 --> 00:08:20.200
-Yeah. Mm-hmm.
-I didn't know about this.

00:08:20.200 --> 00:08:22.567
That Johnny Carson,
they made a --

00:08:22.567 --> 00:08:25.701
They made a record?
-Yeah, they did a Johnny Carson.

00:08:25.701 --> 00:08:29.033
They decided to record him,
Johnny Carson, live.

00:08:29.033 --> 00:08:31.434
And the funniest thing
is that it did --

00:08:31.434 --> 00:08:33.634
it did so bad that --

00:08:33.634 --> 00:08:37.267
The joke is that more records
were returned

00:08:37.267 --> 00:08:39.067
than Casablanca put out.

00:08:39.067 --> 00:08:42.133
You know what I mean?
Which is insane.

00:08:42.133 --> 00:08:45.834
But, you know, and that's --
that's where me and --

00:08:45.834 --> 00:08:47.434
me and Neil Bogart --

00:08:47.434 --> 00:08:48.968
Jeremy Jordan plays him.

00:08:48.968 --> 00:08:50.501
That's where we get
into this argument,

00:08:50.501 --> 00:08:51.801
like, in the movie.

00:08:51.801 --> 00:08:53.467
Like, there's a part
in the movie

00:08:53.467 --> 00:08:55.434
where we're just --
we're just butting heads

00:08:55.434 --> 00:08:58.801
because I don't know
where this is going.

00:08:58.801 --> 00:09:01.567
I'm like, "Dude,
I followed you all the way.

00:09:01.567 --> 00:09:04.334
I'm your brother.
But we are losing --

00:09:04.334 --> 00:09:06.334
I can't. I don't have --
Nobody has any money."

00:09:06.334 --> 00:09:08.200
They didn't have any money.

00:09:08.200 --> 00:09:10.334
They were $7 million in debt
when they did that.

00:09:10.334 --> 00:09:13.167
-Even with Donna Summer?
-Even with --

00:09:13.167 --> 00:09:16.267
Donna Summer came after.
She came right after that.

00:09:16.267 --> 00:09:20.567
And that's when Donna Summer
saved Casablanca Records.

00:09:20.567 --> 00:09:21.801
-Whew!
-Real talk.

00:09:21.801 --> 00:09:24.100
Real talk. Real talk.
-I want to show a clip.

00:09:24.100 --> 00:09:26.634
-Here's Jay Pharoah
in "Spinning Gold."

00:09:26.634 --> 00:09:28.267
Take a look at this.

00:09:28.267 --> 00:09:30.868
-Neil. Neil!
-What?!

00:09:30.868 --> 00:09:32.801
[ Telephone rings ]

00:09:32.801 --> 00:09:35.167
-What if we were wrong
about Carson?

00:09:35.167 --> 00:09:37.934
-I mean, we're shipping gold.
More.

00:09:37.934 --> 00:09:41.167
Over 750,000 copies already.

00:09:41.167 --> 00:09:43.334
And with the money we're
spending on commercials

00:09:43.334 --> 00:09:46.734
and print ads...
-It's Johnny [bleep] Carson!

00:09:46.734 --> 00:09:49.167
-Nobody understands why the hell
we're even doing it.

00:09:49.167 --> 00:09:51.200
-Then ship more! Spend more!

00:09:51.200 --> 00:09:53.234
Do your job
and make them understand

00:09:53.234 --> 00:09:55.801
this is gonna be the biggest
[bleep] album of the year!

00:09:55.801 --> 00:09:57.868
Okay, folks?
-You've lost your mind.

00:09:57.868 --> 00:10:00.367
Did you not hear
what they said on the phone?

00:10:00.367 --> 00:10:02.367
And they were
on our [bleep] side.

00:10:02.367 --> 00:10:04.133
-Nobody is on our [bleep] side!

00:10:04.133 --> 00:10:05.567
-'Cause nobody understands

00:10:05.567 --> 00:10:07.968
what the [bleep]
you're doing anymore!

00:10:07.968 --> 00:10:09.267
-Whoo!

00:10:09.267 --> 00:10:11.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:11.033 --> 00:10:12.367
Who was that guy?

00:10:12.367 --> 00:10:15.367
-Uh, I'm -- I don't know.
I don't know.

00:10:15.367 --> 00:10:17.167
-Come on. Well done.
-I don't know.

00:10:17.167 --> 00:10:19.400
-Yeah, I know.
That's Jay Pharoah right there!

00:10:19.400 --> 00:10:21.534
-"Spinning Gold"
is in theaters this Friday.

00:10:21.534 --> 00:10:24.133
We'll be right back with
a performance from Coco Jones.

00:10:24.133 --> 00:10:25.634
Stick around, everybody!

